invariant: INV-14
file: quic_config.c
catches: quic_loop_test
reason: ticket_version_ok admits every configuration, so a client starts
  a connection in one QUIC version with a ticket from a connection in
  the other, which RFC 9369 section 5 forbids (rfc9369.txt:268-271), and
  a ticket presented without its version goes out too.
  test/quic_loop_ticket_versions.h requires CH_EINVAL for a version 2
  ticket in a version 1 connection, the reverse, and a ticket version of
  0.

--- old
    return !cfg->resumption || cfg->ticket_quic_version == cfg->quic_original_version;
--- new
    return cfg != NULL;
